        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "An area type of \"floating ice shelf\" indicates where ice shelves are present. Ice shelves are the component of ice sheets that flow over the ocean."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::cfat5fis";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "floating_ice_shelf"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATV9UFZS/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::ATV9UFZS";
        dc:date                "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::ATV9UFZS";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATV9UFZS/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "An area type of \"unfrozen_soil\" means that the soil at the surface is unfrozen. Frozen soil may be present at lower levels within a soil model."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::ATV9UFZS";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "unfrozen_soil"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATV9FRFW/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::ATV9FRFW";
        dc:date                "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::ATV9FRFW";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/ATV9FRFW/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "An area type of \"fresh_free_water\" means a free interface between freshwater and the atmosphere without vegetation or other obstructions."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::ATV9FRFW";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "fresh_free_water"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/c4plfuty/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::c4plfuty";
        dc:date                "2013-07-11 09:54:22.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::c4plfuty";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-07-11 09:54:22.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/c4plfuty/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "A plant that utilizes the C4 carbon fixation pathway in which the CO2 is first bound to a compound containing four carbon atoms before photosynthesis reactions take place. All trees are C3 type. Grasses and crops can be C3 or C4."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::c4plfuty";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "c4_plant_functional_types"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/CFATRIV1/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::CFATRIV1";
        dc:date                "2025-03-19 08:31:35.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::CFATRIV1";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-03-19 08:31:35.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/CFATRIV1/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The area type river means flowing water in a channel that is mainly driven by gravity. It includes streams, creeks and canals but not lakes or seas. It also includes water in a floodplain."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::CFATRIV1";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "river"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/CFATLAIS/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::CFATLAIS";
        dc:date                "2025-03-19 08:31:35.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::CFATLAIS";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-03-19 08:31:35.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/CFATLAIS/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The area type lake_and_inland_sea means a quasi-permanent body of water surrounded by land, which may include certain ponds and reservoirs, but excludes rivers and streams which by gravity convey water into and out of lakes or inland seas or into the ocean."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::CFATLAIS";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "lake_and_inland_sea"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/cfat5ish/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::cfat5ish";
        dc:date                "2023-07-05 16:51:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::cfat5ish";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-07-05 16:51:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/cfat5ish/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/cfat5ish/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "An area type of \"ice sheet\" indicates where ice sheets are present. It includes both grounded ice sheets resting over bedrock and any ice shelves flowing over the ocean that are attached to grounded ice sheets. The ice sheet area type excludes ice-caps and glaciers and any floating ice shelves and ice tongues attached to them, but the land_ice area type includes those as well as the ice_sheet area."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::cfat5ish";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ice_sheet"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/cfat5psl/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::cfat5psl";
        dc:date                "2017-02-21 16:02:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::cfat5psl";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-02-21 16:02:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/cfat5psl/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/cfat5psl/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Primary and secondary land\" is land that is not in use as crop land or pasture land, including forests, grasslands, bare ground and vegetated wetlands. \"Primary land\" is land that has not undergone lulcc (land use or land cover change) due to human disturbance. \"Secondary land\" is land that has previously been used for agriculture, urban development or logging and has subsequently been abandoned. Reference: Hurtt et al. (2011), Climatic Change, 109 - 117, Harmonization of land-use scenarios for the period 1500–2100: 600 years of global gridded annual land-use transitions, wood harvest, and resulting secondary lands, doi: 10.1007/s10584-011-0153-2. \"Primary and secondary land\" refers to land use or management, rather than to specific categories of vegetation cover, e.g. the primary and secondary succession of plant species."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::cfat5psl";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "primary_and_secondary_land"@en .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/CFAT11SC/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P29::CFAT11SC";
        dc:date                "2023-07-05 16:51:32.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P29::CFAT11SC";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-07-05 16:51:32.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P29/current/CFAT11SC/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "This area type complements the \"convective_cloud\" area type, which is the other major category of cloud. The \"cloud\" area type is a more general term and includes both convective_cloud and stratiform_cloud types."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P29::CFAT11SC";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "stratiform_cloud"@en .

